 "purpose": "Input objects for column arithmetic ('rooster') and long division step by step ('staart').",
 "details": "RoosterInvoer lets the child fill the cells of a column sum (add, subtract, multiply, with a carry row, typing direction, decimal comma, place-value letters E T H); StaartInvoer builds a long division by answering one small question per step (divide, multiply, subtract, bring down), with two attempts per step. Both follow the input-object protocol (hoogte, knoppen, teken, toets, hulp, rijen; attributes melding, melding_rol, fouten, diagnose, cursor_pos, hint) and check themselves (geen_tweede_kans) step by step; the Oefenaar only checks the final answer, uses `fouten` and diagnose, and in tests the rows via rijen(). The sums come from kern models (v.model: a Rooster or Staartdeling object); the explanations come from the topic (o.kolom_hulp, o.stap_fout). terminal/beta.py draws the same objects in a bordered panel (in_vak).",
 "module_docstring": "Invullen in een rooster (cijferen onder elkaar) en de staartdeling stap voor stap.",
